ALGORITHM:

1) Start the program.

2) Read the number of charging stations (vertices) and connections (edges).

3) Create an adjacency list to represent the graph.

4) Read the connections between charging stations.

5) Display the available vertices and accept the starting vertex.

6) Initialize all vertices as unvisited.

7) Perform DFS from the selected starting vertex and display the traversal order.

8) Mark all vertices visited during DFS as reachable.

9) Display the reachable vertices and identify unvisited vertices.

10) Check the adjacency list to identify isolated vertices.

11)Perform BFS from the selected starting vertex.

12) Assign level 0 to the starting vertex and calculate the level of each reachable vertex.

13) Count and display the total number of reachable vertices.

14) Stop the program.
